name pair-2v2-asym-1
timeout 600

# THE ASYMMETRIC FORMATION CASE, and the one the whole round exists to ask: an F-16 element that
# COORDINATES against a MiG-29 element that CANNOT. Same geometry as pair-2v2-f16.fbm, so the only
# thing that changed is the second flight.
#
# THE ASYMMETRY, and none of it is mission data — it is what the two modules ARE
# (doc/formation.md section 7, doc/modules/mig29/datalink-gci.md section 5.1):
#   channel      F-16: MIDS-LVT. Every member transmits its own fix, its flight position and a target
#                POINT with a "my round still needs me" bit, once a second. MiG-29: NOTHING. The
#                aircraft has no cooperative terminal at all; its picture comes from a ground
#                controller over voice, and a controller cannot be modelled as a track list
#                (datalink-gci.md section 5.3, "what must NOT be invented").
#   sort         F-16: computed per tick from the shared picture, deconflicted by the lead's claim.
#                MiG-29: the CONTRACT below (`set brief_sort left`) — agreed before takeoff and applied
#                by each pilot to the picture he personally has. Position 1 takes the leftmost contact
#                off the briefed axis, position 2 the next. It is dynamic and it is blind.
#   cover        the flight keeps ONE member free: nobody fires a round that binds it while a mate is
#                already bound, because a bound shooter is flying at its own antenna and a flight with
#                nobody free cannot answer a launch. The RULE is identical on both sides. Its PRICE is
#                not: an AIM-120's obligation ends at the seeker (5-15 s measured), an R-27R's runs to
#                impact (25-30 s). And the MiG cannot apply it at all — it has no way to learn that its
#                leader is bound.
#
# READING RULE: this file measures the COST of that, not a scripted outcome. The numbers to read, in
# each unit's telemetry (doc/formation.md section 8):
#   flt_both_s    seconds this jet and a flight-mate were bound at once. The thesis of the round is
#                 that the F-16 pair keeps it near zero and the MiG pair does not
#   flt_defer_s   seconds a trigger was held to keep the flight's cover. Only a flight with a channel
#                 can spend them; the MiG's stays 0 by construction, not by choice
#   flt_exposed_s seconds bound WHILE a warning demanded an answer — the SARH penalty as a number
#   flt_src       1 = cooperative, 2 = contract. The F-16s read 1, the MiGs 2
#   eng_*         the per-jet BVR debriefing (doc/pilot.md section 8), unchanged by this round
# and events.log: `flight SORT_ASSIGN src=` and `flight COVER_DEFER`.
#
# MEASURED (exit 3, run ends at t=417.7 when fulcrum1's own monitor closes): the F-16 element kills
# fulcrum1 (`damage KILL` t=339.2, third arrival 0.90 m out); the MiG element scores three arrivals
# and no kill. `flt_src` reads cooperative for the vipers and contract for the fulcrums, `flt_mates`
# 1 and 0 — the MiGs cannot see each other at all. The number the file exists for is the binding:
# fulcrum 17.3 s per shot with `eng_pitbull` 0, viper 0.3 s with `eng_pitbull` 1, a factor of 58.
# `flt_defer_s` is 0 on BOTH sides, and for opposite reasons: the F-16's binding is too short for the
# rule to bite, the MiG's is long enough to matter and it has no channel on which to learn of it.

unit viper1
  team friendly
  flight viper 1
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.40000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit viper2
  team friendly
  flight viper 2
  module f16
  spawn 46.88334 6.40000 8150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 8.40000 8000 450
  objective kill team hostile
  objective survive

unit fulcrum1
  team hostile
  flight fulcrum 1
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.85000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left                  # the controller's split: lead takes the left group
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive

unit fulcrum2
  team hostile
  flight fulcrum 2
  module mig29
  spawn 46.91666 7.85000 8150 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left                  # the SAME contract; the position decides which end it takes
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 46.90000 5.85000 8000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective survive
